    becomes load-bearing.
  - [1mES modules[0m — [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m, [38;5;153msettings.js[39m does [38;5;153mexport const settings[39m. Real module boundary, no
    globals, explicit dependency. Costs: ES modules are blocked by CORS on [38;5;153mfile://[39m, so opening [38;5;153mindex.html[39m directly stops
    working — you'd need a local server.

  Both are cheap to swap later; this only touches two small files either way.

  [1mRecommendation: ES modules.[0m You asked for a settings [3mmodule[0m, and this gives you an actual one with an explicit import
  instead of an implicit global plus a load-order rule. The [38;5;153mfile://[39m cost is the thing to weigh — if you currently open
  [38;5;153mindex.html[39m by double-clicking it, say so and I'll take the script-tag option instead.
